# Which takes more lives worldwide: suicide or homicide?
subtitle: "Pick which takes more lives worldwide, suicide or homicide, then see the gap drawn to scale and why the news makes it feel the other way round."
tags: ["health","epidemiology"]
format: quiz
thumb: "question \"Which takes more lives worldwide?\""

## Which takes more lives worldwide: suicide or homicide?
sources:
    - id: owid_s
      title: Suicide rate (both sexes); Number of suicides
      authors: Our World in Data, from the WHO Global Health Estimates
      year: 2024
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/suicide-rate
      finding: world suicide death rate about 9.1 per 100,000 in 2021; about 718,000 suicides in 2021
    - id: owid_h
      title: Homicide rate
      authors: Our World in Data, from the UN Office on Drugs and Crime
      year: 2025
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/homicide-rate-unodc
      finding: world homicide rate about 5.5 per 100,000 in 2021, 6.9 in 2000 and 5.1 in 2024
    - id: owid_fall
      title: The global suicide rate has fallen since the 1990s, but the death toll is still high
      authors: Hannah Ritchie (Our World in Data), from IHME Global Burden of Disease
      year: 2026
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/data-insights/the-global-suicide-rate-has-fallen-since-the-1990s-but-the-death-toll-is-still-high
      finding: global suicide rates have fallen by an estimated 40% since the 1990s, from 15 to 9 deaths per 100,000
    - id: owid_news
      title: Does the news reflect what we die from?
      authors: Hannah Ritchie, Tuna Acisu and Edouard Mathieu (Our World in Data)
      year: 2025
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/does-the-news-reflect-what-we-die-from
      finding: 'US deaths in 2023 against coverage in the New York Times, Washington Post and Fox News: homicides received 43 times more coverage than their share of deaths'

    box opt_s "Suicide" #2f6b8f x 300 y 430 width 300 height 110 font_size 52 hidden true
    box opt_h "Homicide" #b5482e x 700 y 430 width 300 height 110 font_size 52 hidden true
    shape then_bar dashed #2f6b8f shape rect x 300 y 465 width 220 height 360 style.opacity 0.6 style.stroke_width 2 hidden true
    text then_l "1990s: ~15" #2f6b8f cites ["owid_fall"] x 300 y 615 font_size 34 hidden true
    text fall_s "−40%" #2f6b8f cites ["owid_fall"] x 500 y 573 font_size 52 hidden true
    shape bar_s #2f6b8f shape rect x 300 y 394.2 width 220 height 218.39999999999998 style.fill #2f6b8f style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.45 hidden true
    shape bar_h #b5482e shape rect x 700 y 351 width 220 height 132 style.fill #b5482e style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.45 hidden true
    text val_s "9.1" #2f6b8f cites ["owid_s"] x 300 y 463.4 font_size 60 hidden true
    text val_h "5.5" #b5482e cites ["owid_h"] x 700 y 377 font_size 60 hidden true
    text unit "per 100,000 a year" #8f887c x 700 y 447 font_size 30 hidden true

    card title "Suicide or homicide: which takes more lives?"

Around the world, which takes more lives each year: suicide, or homicide?
    draw opt_s opt_h parallel true

    ask "Tap the one you think takes more lives." choose ["opt_s","opt_h"] answer opt_s store c
        right: Suicide does, by a wide margin.
        wrong: Think about which one you rarely hear about.

    move opt_s opt_h by [0,-200] duration 0.8

Worldwide, about nine people in every hundred thousand die by suicide each year: more than seven hundred thousand lives.
    draw unit bar_s val_s

Homicide takes about five and a half per hundred thousand. So suicide claims about two-thirds more lives.
    draw bar_h val_h

And it is not because suicide is rising. In the early 1990s the rate was about fifteen; it has fallen by some forty percent.
    draw then_bar then_l fall_s

    erase then_bar then_l fall_s unit

So why does murder feel like the bigger threat? It is news. In three big American news outlets, homicide got forty-three times more coverage than its share of deaths.
    icon news size 120 set twemoji x 600 y 570 icon_look picture of newspaper
    text news_l "43× coverage" #b5482e cites ["owid_news"] x 800 y 570 font_size 46

Suicide rarely makes the news, so the larger bar is the one we hardly see.
    highlight bar_s effect underline

    erase news news_l

Behind that bar are people. If this touches you or someone close, talk to someone, or find a helpline near you.
    text help "findahelpline.com" #2f6b8f x 720 y 560 font_size 46

